  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reaching Isolated Communities the African Way</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to expand the reach of much-needed relief and development assistance to people in isolated communities in cooperation with government and civil society organisations with funding from East Africa. The aim is to establish a resource hub based in Kenya tasked to fund interventions, to recruit and support staff from the East African region and communicate externally to potential funding partners. The hub will be capacitated by designing and implementing a fundraising strategy and receive training to be able to fund operations to help vulnerable people and to support the recruited staff.</narrative>
  </description>
